# Mahjong Autotable — environment template for docker compose.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is gitignored
# (and .dockerignored) so nothing here is ever committed or baked into an
# image. Docker Compose auto-loads `.env` from this directory for the
# `${VAR}` substitutions in docker-compose.yml / docker-compose.postgres.yml.
#
# Easiest (idempotent — writes/keeps a stable JWT key):
#   ./scripts/compose-bootstrap.sh
#   docker compose up -d --build
#
# Manual equivalent:
#   cp .env.example .env
#   echo "JWT_SIGNING_KEY=$(openssl rand -base64 48)" >> .env
#   docker compose up -d --build
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — JWT signing key
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The container runs ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production, which refuses to
# boot without a stable HMAC signing key. (A per-process random key would
# silently invalidate every JWT on restart — see JwtSigningKeyProvider.cs
# and docs/jwt-rotation.md §7.) docker-compose.yml injects this value as
# `Authentication__JwtSigningKeys__0` and fails fast if it is unset/empty.
#
# Generate a fresh base64 key (~48 bytes recommended) and KEEP IT STABLE
# across restarts — rotating it invalidates all previously issued JWTs:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 48
#
# Then set it below (uncomment and paste your own value — do NOT reuse the
# illustrative format shown here, and never commit a real key):
# JWT_SIGNING_KEY=replace-with-output-of-openssl-rand-base64-48

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — build metadata
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Surfaced by /health as buildSha. Defaults to "local" when unset.
# BUILD_SHA=local

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL — Postgres overlay (docker-compose.postgres.yml)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only used when you add `-f docker-compose.postgres.yml`. The defaults
# below are DEV-ONLY; override POSTGRES_PASSWORD (and keep it in sync with
# the connection string the overlay builds) for anything touching real users.
# POSTGRES_DB=mahjong_autotable
# POSTGRES_USER=mahjong
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=mahjong
